          "our_approach": "Recommend: (1) instrument current rescue-pickup and distribution routes to establish a baseline (route count, miles, transit time to shelf, and — critically — a spoilage/shrinkage rate HFB does not currently publish); (2) pilot a dynamic route-optimization + first-expiry-first-out (FEFO) dispatch layer on perishable/produce routes specifically, since produce is 47% of output and the most time-sensitive category; (3) train any routing model on HFB's own historical driver routes (not just theoretical shortest-path), mirroring the insight behind both UPS ORION and the Amazon Last Mile Challenge that real driver route data outperforms naive distance optimization; (4) report gains against the baseline in miles, gallons, and — using HFB's own implied ~1.26 lbs/meal ratio — meals preserved, so results are comparable to HFB's own published impact metrics rather than only logistics units.",
